From 947431d9b757698bbceef8357532c85b6ea5edba Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Vortiago <atle@havso.net>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 09:22:10 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] tests: backend-sampler tests for a dist that picks on the CPU

dist has no backend implementation since the Gumbel-max pick. A chain that ends in dist
now runs its filters on the backend and picks on the CPU, so no backend token is set.

- The tests that read a backend dist token now sample with the chain.
- dist_and_cpu: a CPU dist that was never set on the context picks what the context's
  chain picks, with the same seed (it used two seeds before).
- The multi-output tests check each pick against a new dist(seed) that has accepted the
  same count, over the row's candidates. This replaces the mt19937 inverse-CDF reference.
  It still checks that a row sampled without accept, or a state restored with
  llama_sampler_copy, does not move the noise, and that each sequence uses its own seed.
- No backend sampler fills probs now; the probs checks are gone.

The old test fails 10 of 19 cases on this branch; this one passes 19 of 19 (Qwen3-0.6B,
CUDA). Against rel3 it fails 6, the cases that check the new pick.

